    "evidence": "Unpatched run output: \"[POV] persisted fullName reaching Hadoop path sink = /pov/../../../../../../../../tmp/dolphin_pwn/pov_evil_dir\", \"[POV] normalized HDFS target = /tmp/dolphin_pwn/pov_evil_dir\", \"OK (1 test)\", FINAL_EXIT=0. Patched-simulation run (added `if (fullName.contains(\"..\")) return VERIFY_PARAMETER_NAME_FAILED;` before verifyResource in createDirectory): \"createDirectory result = The file name verify failed\", \"Wanted but not invoked\" (resourcesMapper.insert), \"FAILURES!!! Tests run: 1, Failures: 1\", POV_EXIT=1. Patch was reverted afterward; git status shows a clean product tree (changes only under .security-pipeline/).",
    "expected_vulnerable_behavior": "On the unpatched code, createDirectory accepts the attacker-controlled traversal parent directory \"/pov/../../../../../../../../tmp/dolphin_pwn\"; the resulting fullName \"/pov/../../../../../../../../tmp/dolphin_pwn/pov_evil_dir\" is persisted via resourcesMapper.insert(...) and passed to HadoopUtils.getHdfsFileName(...), and normalizes to /tmp/dolphin_pwn/pov_evil_dir which escapes the tenant root /dolphinscheduler/123/resources/. The JUnitCore run reports OK (1 test) and exits 0. After a correct patch (rejecting or normalizing the traversal), insert is never reached (or fullName no longer contains \"/../\"), the Mockito verification/assertion fails, and the command exits non-zero.",
    "notes": "Execution constraints discovered: (1) Each run_in_docker.sh invocation is a fresh container; only /workspace/repo persists (the image's /root/.m2 baseline is read-only-ish and new installs/downloads do not persist). (2) Network and maven-dependency-plugin are NOT reliably available at run time, so the classpath is pre-captured once into .security-pipeline/pov/cp.txt; its external (non-DolphinScheduler) jars live in the image .m2, and sibling DS modules are taken from freshly built worktree target/classes. (3) The module's 67 tests are JUnit4+PowerMock but the image has no junit-vintage-engine, so Surefire's JUnit5 platform provider discovers 0 JUnit4 tests (`mvn test -Dtest=ResourcesServiceTest` reports \"Tests run: 0\"); the runner therefore executes the POV via org.junit.runner.JUnitCore. mockito is pinned to 2.21.0 (no mockStatic), so static mocking requires PowerMock. run_pov.sh copies the POV into the api test tree only for compilation and removes it on exit (trap), keeping the product test tree clean; the canonical POV file remains under .security-pipeline/pov/. Build uses -Djacoco.skip=true and a shell rm of target dirs (maven-clean-plugin is not cached offline).",
    "pov_command": "bash .security-pipeline/pov/run_pov.sh",
    "pov_path": ".security-pipeline/pov/ResourcesPathTraversalPovTest.java",
